    "id": "00c93f30-28dc-451c-abe1-069d996553ef",
    "slug": "ai-cad-tools-compared-2026-text-to-cad-copilots-and-where-each-fits",
    "title": "AI CAD Tools Compared (2026): Text-to-CAD, Copilots, and Where Each Fits",
    "excerpt": "AI CAD now covers four kinds of tool. See how text-to-CAD generators, copilots, script tools and drawing automation differ, and which fits your workflow.",
    "content": "\"AI CAD\" now covers at least four different kinds of tool, and comparing them as if they were one category is how teams pick the wrong one. A generator that makes a new part from a sentence solves a different problem than a copilot that searches your existing parts library.\n\nThis guide sorts the 2026 landscape by what each tool produces, so you can match it to your workflow. Details on other tools come from public reviews and vendor pages as of October 2026; confirm current features and pricing before you buy.\n\n## The four types of AI CAD tool\n\n1. **Text-to-CAD generators** create a new 3D part from a written prompt.\n2. **Engineering copilots** answer questions, search parts, or reason about designs inside an existing workflow.\n3. **Script and automation tools** write code or macros that drive traditional CAD software.\n4. **Drawing and documentation automation** turns finished models into manufacturing drawings.\n\nA fifth group, text-to-3D mesh generators, makes shapes for visualization and games. They look similar in demos but output differently. We cover that in our guide to text-to-CAD vs text-to-3D.\n\n## Comparison at a glance\n\n| Tool | Type | Typical output | Best for |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| CadXStudio | Text-to-CAD generator plus manual parametric editing and drawings | B-rep parametric models; STEP, STL, OBJ export; multi-part assemblies | Concept-to-manufacturing parts in the browser, from a vague idea to a spec to a model |\n| Zoo | Text-to-CAD and CAD API | Editable B-rep models | Mechanical parts, developers building on an open API |\n| AdamCAD | Text-to-CAD web editor | Parametric models with adjustable sliders | Quick parametric concepts; has an Onshape plugin |\n| Leo AI | Engineering copilot | Answers, part search, design reasoning | Teams with existing CAD data and vaults |\n| CADGPT | Script generation | Scripts for traditional CAD platforms | Engineers automating repetitive modelling |\n| DraftAid | Drawing automation | Manufacturing drawings | Drafting departments |\n| Hunyuan, Tripo | Text-to-3D | Mostly mesh geometry | Visual concepts and quick shapes |\n\n## What to check before choosing\n\n- **Output type.** Parametric B-rep (STEP) can be edited and sent to a supplier. Mesh (STL, OBJ) is fine for printing but hard to edit.\n- **Editability.** Can you change a dimension later without regenerating the whole model?\n- **Assemblies.** Many tools generate single parts only. If your product has several, check this first.\n- **Drawings.** Do you get 2D engineering drawings from the same tool?\n- **Manufacturability.** Does the tool understand wall thickness, draft, and process limits?\n- **Existing files.** Can it start from a STEP or CAD file you already have?\n- **Where it runs.** Browser, desktop plug-in, or API.\n\n## Where CadXStudio fits, and where it does not\n\nCadXStudio is built for concept-stage and iterative design. The Design Engine puts text-to-3D generation, full manual parametric editing, and 3D-to-2D drawing generation in one browser tab with no install. Brainstorm turns a vague idea into a detailed spec before Build creates the model. Version 2.0 generates DFM-ready models, and assemblies live in one workspace.\n\nTwo honest limits: CadXStudio is text-to-CAD only today, with no CAM or G-code output, and STEP file import is on the roadmap rather than live (image input already works). If your workflow starts from existing CAD files, that matters.\n\n## Pricing snapshot (as of September 2026)\n\n| Plan | Price | Includes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Free | $0 | Limited AI design, limited drawing generation, B-rep CAD models, STEP export |\n| Pro | $20/month | Extended AI usage, unlimited drawing and rendering, collaboration |\n| Engineer | $49/month | Maximum AI usage, advanced design history, SSO and priority support |\n\n## How to decide in 10 minutes\n\n1. Write the part you need next month in one paragraph.\n2. Run it through two tools from different categories.\n3. Open each result in your CAD software. Can you edit it?\n4. Check the export format your supplier or printer needs.\n\nReady to test it? [Run your first prompt free on CadXStudio](https://cadxstudio.in).",
