    "title": "From CAD to Photorealistic Rendering — Directly in Your Browser",
    "excerpt": "From CAD to Photorealistic Rendering — Directly in Your Browser",
    "content": "# From CAD to Photorealistic Rendering — Directly in Your Browser\n\n**Turn engineering models into product visuals without leaving CadXStudio.**\n\nDesigning a product doesn't end when the CAD model is complete. Engineers and product designers often need to communicate what a design will actually look like — materials, finishes, proportions, lighting, and overall form — before it ever reaches production.\n\nTraditionally, that means exporting the CAD model into another rendering or visualization tool.\n\nWe wanted to remove that extra step.\n\nWith **CadXStudio Rendering**, you can now take your CAD model directly into a browser-based rendering environment and create high-quality product visuals without leaving the platform.\n\n---\n\n## One CAD workflow, from design to visualization\n\nCadXStudio is built around a simple idea:\n\n> **Your engineering model should stay connected to everything you do with it.**\n\nGenerate or edit your CAD model, then move directly into rendering.\n\nNo exporting to another application.  \nNo rebuilding the scene somewhere else.  \nNo breaking the design workflow just to create a visual.\n\nThe same model you engineer can become the model you visualize.\n\n---\n\n## From engineering geometry to product visualization\n\nThe rendering workflow is designed to give you control over how the final product looks.\n\nYou can work with:\n\n- **Materials**\n- **Studio environments**\n- **Lighting**\n- **Render quality**\n- **Ray-traced output**\n\nThis makes it possible to move from a basic CAD representation to something much closer to a finished product visualization.\n\n---\n\n## Ray-traced rendering in the browser\n\nCadXStudio uses browser-based ray tracing to produce progressively refined renders.\n\nInstead of waiting for a completely separate rendering workflow, you can start rendering directly from the CAD environment and watch the image improve as more samples are accumulated.\n\nThe rendering system provides different quality levels depending on what you need:\n\n**Draft** for quick previews.\n\n**Studio** for higher-quality visualization.\n\n**Max** for detailed hero renders.\n\nThis makes the same workflow useful for both rapid design iteration and polished product presentation.\n\n---\n\n## Designed for engineers, not just renders\n\nThe interesting part isn't simply creating a pretty image.\n\nThe CAD model remains the source of truth.\n\nThat means you can continue changing the engineering design and then visualize the updated version again.\n\nThis creates a much tighter loop:\n\n```text\nEngineering Intent\n        ↓\nParametric CAD\n        ↓\nDesign Iteration\n        ↓\nRendering\n        ↓\nReview & Communication\n        ↓\nFurther Engineering",
