    "excerpt": " Drawings from Any CAD Model in Seconds",
    "content": "# From CAD to Engineering Drawings in One Click\n\nEngineering drawings are essential for turning a 3D model into something that can actually be manufactured. However, creating production-style drawings is often a repetitive and time-consuming task that requires manual view placement, dimensioning, annotations, and documentation.\n\nAt **CadX**, we're building a faster way.\n\nOur latest **Engineering Drawing Engine** automatically converts generated CAD models into professional engineering drawings directly in the browser. With a single click, CadX creates clean documentation that engineers can review, share, and export in seconds.\n\n---\n\n## Why Engineering Drawings Still Matter\n\nNo matter how advanced CAD modeling becomes, engineering drawings remain the universal language of manufacturing.\n\nThey communicate:\n\n- Overall geometry\n- Critical dimensions\n- Hole locations\n- Hidden features\n- Manufacturing notes\n- Standard orthographic views\n- Assembly documentation\n\nEvery manufactured product eventually relies on accurate engineering documentation.\n\n---\n\n## One Click. Complete Documentation.\n\nCadX automatically generates engineering drawings directly from your CAD model, eliminating hours of repetitive drafting work.\n\nCurrent capabilities include:\n\n- Automatic orthographic projections\n- Isometric view generation\n- Automatic dimension placement\n- Center marks\n- Hidden line generation\n- General manufacturing notes\n- Professional title block\n- First & Third Angle projection support\n- Multi-sheet drawing generation\n- PDF export\n\n---\n\n## Assembly Drawings Included\n\nCadX doesn't stop at individual components.\n\nComplex assemblies can automatically generate:\n\n- Complete assembly drawings\n- Individual engineering drawings for every component\n- Multi-page documentation packages\n\nThis significantly reduces the time required to document large mechanical designs.\n\n---\n\n## Built Entirely in the Browser\n\nUnlike traditional CAD software, CadX runs entirely in your browser.\n\nNo installation.\n\nNo workstation setup.\n\nNo plugins.\n\nSimply generate your model, review it, and create engineering drawings in seconds.\n\n---\n\n## What's Coming Next\n\nOur roadmap is focused on making engineering documentation even smarter.\n\nUpcoming features include:\n\n- Automatic datum generation\n- Centerlines\n- GD&T annotations\n- Intelligent drawing layouts\n- Automatic section views\n- Detail views\n- Hole tables\n- Bill of Materials (BOM)\n- Exploded assembly drawings\n- Manufacturing-ready documentation packages\n\n---\n\n## Beyond AI CAD Generation\n\nGenerating CAD models is only part of the engineering workflow.\n\nOur vision is to automate the entire documentation process—from design generation to manufacturing-ready deliverables.\n\nSoon, you'll be able to upload existing CAD models, including STEP files, and automatically generate professional engineering drawings with a single click.\n\nWhether your model was created in SolidWorks, CATIA, NX, Creo, Fusion 360, Inventor, Onshape, or FreeCAD, CadX aims to simplify engineering documentation for every mechanical engineer.\n\n---\n\n## The Future of Engineering Documentation\n\nImagine a workflow where documentation takes seconds instead of hours.\n\n```\nCAD Model\n      ↓\nGenerate Engineering Drawing\n      ↓\nAssembly Documentation\n      ↓\nIndividual Part Drawings\n      ↓\nExport PDF\n```\n\nThat's the future we're building.\n\nAt CadX, our mission is simple:\n\n**Spend more time engineering. Spend less time documenting.**\n\n\n\n",
