    "content": "AI is changing how engineers and product teams create 3D models. Instead of spending hours building geometry manually, a user can now describe a part in plain language and generate a CAD model much faster.\n\nThis approach is often called text-to-CAD or AI CAD. It works by turning a written prompt into structured design instructions, which are then converted into editable 3D geometry. The result is a model that can be refined, measured, and used for further engineering work.\n\nFor example, a prompt like “create a simple wall-mounted bottle holder with mounting holes” can be transformed into a CAD-ready design. The user can then adjust dimensions, change features, or iterate on the design without starting from scratch.\n\nThis workflow is especially useful for hardware startups, mechanical engineers, and product designers who need to move quickly from idea to prototype. It reduces repetitive modeling work and helps teams test concepts faster.\n\nAt CadXStudio, we focus on making this process simple, fast, and practical for real engineering use. Our goal is to help teams generate editable CAD models from text prompts and speed up product development from concept to prototype.\n\nIf you are looking for a faster way to create CAD models, AI-powered design workflows are becoming one of the most promising tools in modern product development.",
